# CODEOWNERS for Liquifact/Liquifact-frontend
#
# Automatically requests review from the mapped owner(s) whenever a pull
# request touches a matching path. Later (more specific) rules win, so
# sensitive subpaths are listed after their broader parent directories.
# See: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners
#
# NOTE: the handles below are placeholders. Replace every @OWNER-* entry
# with real GitHub usernames or teams (e.g. @Liquifact/wallet) before this
# file can assign reviewers — GitHub silently skips a rule whose owner
# does not exist or lacks repo access. See CONTRIBUTING.md for details.

# Fallback: anything not matched by a more specific rule below.
*                           @OWNER-CORE

# Application routes and pages.
/app/                       @OWNER-APP

# Shared UI components.
/components/                @OWNER-COMPONENTS

# Wallet integration (Freighter, signing, connection flows) — sensitive.
/lib/wallet/                @OWNER-WALLET

# API client layer.
/lib/api/                   @OWNER-API

# Security headers configuration — sensitive.
/lib/securityHeaders.mjs    @OWNER-SECURITY

# Documentation.
/docs/                      @OWNER-DOCS
CONTRIBUTING.md             @OWNER-DOCS

# CI/CD workflows and repo automation — sensitive.
/.github/                   @OWNER-CI
